WEBVTT

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:12.750
Bug!

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.320
Crashbug!

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.280
Bug!

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:24.820
Bug!

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.690
Bug!

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.310
Bug!

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:34.550
Bug!

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:37.550
Bug!

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:38.300
Bug!

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.850
Crashbug!

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:44.580
Cleaning.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:47.220
Crashbug!

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.400
What are you doing?

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:53.210
Bug!

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:58.700
You’re going to keep following me?

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.700
I can’t leave
even if I wanted to.

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:06.670
But if my memories return,
I may learn how to leave.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:10.570
How will you get
your memories back?

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.710
By gathering Numbers.

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:14.170
Numbers?

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:17.890
And you expect me
to do that?

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:21.150
Yuma is talking to himself again.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:24.600
Do you really think there’s
a ghost duelist?

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.550
I definitely don’t
want to do that!

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:29.060
So stop following me!

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:32.780
Maybe Yusei lost his mind.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:35.150
Observation #2:

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:36.810
You’re weird.

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:37.780
I’ll remember that.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:39.780
I’m not weird!

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:42.700
What’s that?

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.000
What’s wrong, sis?

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.750
It’s gone.

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:49.320
My article is gone.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:51.000
There’s a virus in the system.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.010
There’s only one hour
until the deadline.

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:55.920
Calm down, sis.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.430
I’m going to miss the deadline...

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.750
When my sister acts like this...

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:02.430
We should run away.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:04.720
Yuma!

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:08.100
Find me a scoop immediately!

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:13.900
When she’s like that,
she’s out of control.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.240
Anyway, it’s really congested.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:18.310
Yeah.

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:22.280
All the lights are red,
and the monorail isn’t moving.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:23.950
What?

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:27.760
Lucky! Juice is popping out!

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.490
Wait a second, Yuma!

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:31.470
You can’t take them!

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:33.060
I’ll give them back—

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:35.070
Cleaning.

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:37.470
Stop it! Let me go!

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:41.720
The city’s systems went down today—

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:43.350
My article is gone.

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:45.060
Thanks for the meal!

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.080
I missed my deadline.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:50.380
A cleaning robot grabbed me!

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:52.590
The same thing happened to me.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:54.020
What?

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:55.980
It was on the news.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:58.020
Big trouble.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:00.300
The cleaning robots
and vending machines malfunctioned.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:01.990
And the monorail stopped.

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:04.950
It just recently returned to normal.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.320
I see.

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:08.970
I’m not the only
one who lost data.

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:09.910
Sis?

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:11.370
Something smells.

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:15.940
No!

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:17.840
I smell a case!

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:19.140
I have to pull myself together!

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:20.340
Replenishing energy!

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:22.300
Hey, that’s mine!

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.320
I have to investigate right away!

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:33.350
So this is how humans
replenish energy.

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:36.520
And the energy...

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.800
After you replenish, you must emit.

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:43.970
I have a lot going on!

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:47.660
Why can’t I enter?

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.870
You idiot! Of course you can’t!

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:52.010
Emitting energy is a secret!

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:54.580
If you see me doing
this, I’ll die!

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:55.750
What?

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:58.600
I didn’t know it was
that important.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:00.840
Observation #3:

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:04.200
Humans have a combo
of eating and emitting.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:07.510
But if they’re seen
emitting, they’ll die.

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:08.970
Be quiet!

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:10.930
But that’s strange.

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:13.980
Humans have this perfect combo...

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:18.820
So why is your
dueling so imperfect?

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:21.400
What do you mean by that?

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.490
To be honest,
your dueling is bad.

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:26.410
Shut up!

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:28.590
There’s no such thing
as a perfect person!

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:30.790
We’re interesting because we fail!

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:34.790
If I fail,
I’ll lose many things.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:39.750
You can’t kattobing
if you’re afraid to fail!

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:43.270
A ghost will never understand that!

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:55.730
I know I had
an important mission.

00:04:56.210 --> 00:05:00.860
I was supposed to take
over Yuma’s body to fulfill that mission.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:07.330
But my memories were
scattered in 99 Number cards.

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:11.660
If I don’t gather the Numbers,
my memories won’t return.

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:16.960
Numbers have the power to take over
and control people.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:23.630
That Number controlled that boy,
but I couldn’t control Yuma.

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:25.180
Why?

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:29.090
Did something stop me?

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:41.810
Where am I?

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:46.700
Bug!

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:55.440
Crashbug!

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:57.000
Bug!

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:03.710
Whether it’s rain, wind,
blizzard or the scorching sun

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.840
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:09.890
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:14.020
Freedom begins by accepting differences
Dance and create the universe

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:21.400
In truth, I was sad
until I met you

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:28.060
I lied, thinking it was
easier to be alone

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:34.490
Even though we don’t like
the same books or hobbies

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:38.370
You’re the only one
who agreed with me

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:41.500
Joy and sadness and anger
and do re mi fa so la ti do

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.510
There’s no harmony and scenario
without differences

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.590
Everyone is not the same

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:51.590
That’s the reason for living

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:56.850
Even if the sounds
are dissonant at times

00:06:56.850 --> 00:07:02.270
That’s why I never give up
I believe my strength will get me through

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:06.330
I travel to
the edge of the world

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:09.990
The sights I see
with you are the truth

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:13.310
Whether it’s rain, wind,
blizzard or the scorching sun

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:16.370
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:19.460
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:23.580
Freedom begins by accepting differences
Dance and create the universe

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:31.450
Ouch!

00:07:32.370 --> 00:07:37.060
To Summarize, It’s a Case!!

00:07:32.370 --> 00:07:37.060
Number 3:

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:37.060
To Summarize, It’s a Case!!

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:37.060
Hooray! He’s no longer here!

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:40.020
Oh no!

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:43.480
I’m late!

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:46.690
I made it...

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:49.440
Listen, everyone.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:54.690
Due to yesterday’s signal problems,
the school’s host computer is still down.

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:56.560
Therefore, we can’t use our textbooks.

00:07:56.560 --> 00:07:57.620
We still don’t know what
caused the incident—

00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:58.890
Right!

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:00.780
I’ll answer that!

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:04.550
Does the class representative know something?

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:05.510
Yes!

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:09.230
With my programming
skills, it was easy.

00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:15.300
To summarize, someone broke into the city’s host computer
and caused yesterday’s problems.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:17.310
I used my skills
to find out where—

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:18.260
Teacher!

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:20.770
Let’s have a duel tournament instead!

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:22.980
Let me think about that...

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:25.230
Let’s do that!

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:26.680
Hooray!

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:29.190
I can kattobing the entire day!

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:29.950
Hooray!

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:31.180
Nice, Mr. Ukyo!

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:31.940
You’re so reasonable!

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:35.040
Just when I had the spotlight...

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:35.870
In that case...

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:37.010
Yuma!

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:39.250
To summarize, duel me!

00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:41.370
Sure! I’d like that!

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:45.460
Duel Disk set!

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:48.250
D-Gazer set!

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:51.220
Duel target lock on!

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:57.400
AR Vision Link complete.

00:08:58.270 --> 00:08:59.180
Duel!

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:01.140
Do your best, Yuma!

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:05.600
Yuma, is it true
that you defeated Shark?

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:07.560
Yeah, it’s true!

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:09.590
I don’t believe it.

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:12.070
You can’t even defeat me.

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:14.410
It’s true, class representative!

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:16.030
We’re witnesses!

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:17.430
I see.

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:19.580
So if I win this duel...

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:23.960
To summarize, it means
I’m stronger than Shark!

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:26.670
You keep saying “to summarize.”

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:30.550
It’ll be bad if a sea lion
gets caught in your throat!

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:32.550
Stuck in my throat?

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:35.740
Let’s get started!

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:37.640
I have a Number card!

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:41.220
My Number is missing!

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:42.830
Here I go!

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:44.700
My turn! I draw!

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:50.110
Wait a second!

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:52.760
Go, Crashbug X!

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:55.740
Crashbug!

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:57.450
Attack him directly!

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:00.950
No way...

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:03.600
4000 vs 0.

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:05.250
Yuma...

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:07.220
You totally lost!

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:12.580
I knew Yuma couldn’t beat me
because he gets bad grades.

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:16.290
To summarize,
an idiot can’t win a duel.

00:10:16.290 --> 00:10:17.550
What?

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:19.680
Don’t say that.

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:22.430
Life is
the same as a duel.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:24.720
It never goes as planned.

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:27.100
Just learn from your mistakes.

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:29.100
If you make a mistake...

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:32.060
Let Crashbug eat it.

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:40.030
Crashbug is an electric fairy
that eats people’s bugs.

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:43.490
When it eats too many bugs,
it becomes gigantic.

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:48.620
If you see it under a full moon,
you’ll have a wonderful life.

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:49.880
Teacher!

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:52.960
To summarize, it doesn’t actually exist!

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:55.880
I think it does.

00:10:57.680 --> 00:11:00.340
Yuma, it’s okay to lose!

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:01.590
Learn from your defeats.

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:06.310
Kattobing means that you have
the heart to keep trying!

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:08.320
Mr. Ukyo!

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:09.660
You’re right!

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:11.520
I can always kattobing!

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:16.600
Mr. Ukyo is a great guy.

00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:20.030
Since he’s a match teacher,
he’s smart. And he’s nice.

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:22.960
When I grow up,
I want to be like him!

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:29.700
Hi, Yuma.

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:30.840
Sis?

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:33.170
Do you two wanna
go for a ride?

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:41.120
We’re lucky that yesterday’s
virus didn’t affect many computers.

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:44.300
If it was widespread...

00:11:46.490 --> 00:11:49.480
There would’ve been
total panic in the city.

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:52.190
Total panic?

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:55.450
It’d be more than street lights
and vending machines.

00:11:55.450 --> 00:11:58.570
If it erases
or rewrites bank data...

00:11:58.970 --> 00:12:04.020
...or if the hospital systems
don’t work, it’ll be a disaster.

00:12:04.020 --> 00:12:05.780
Are you serious?

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:07.490
Who would do that?

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:12.750
The computer virus was sent
from your library.

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:18.880
I want you to stake
out the library.

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:21.340
The criminal will
likely show up again!

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:23.330
It sounds fun!

00:12:23.330 --> 00:12:25.550
But why do we
have to do it?

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:27.530
Stop complaining!

00:12:27.530 --> 00:12:29.220
I lost my article!

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:32.470
When I find the culprit,
I’ll use my karate to beat him up!

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:33.900
I’m a black belt!

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:35.960
Listen, Yuma.

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:41.130
Your sister said that the criminal will show up
at the library’s computer area.

00:12:41.130 --> 00:12:43.400
This is so annoying.

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:46.830
C’mon, keep watch!

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:55.310
It’s almost closing time.

00:12:55.310 --> 00:12:57.890
Maybe he’s not coming today.

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:01.840
Yuma, isn’t that...

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:03.840
Class representative!

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:06.120
Something’s suspicious.

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:07.180
Yuma!

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:12.230
Is that a data stick?

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:20.230
What? Is this—

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:22.430
I caught you!

00:13:22.430 --> 00:13:25.200
You’re behind this crime!

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:26.680
You’re wrong!

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:28.130
I’m not the criminal!

00:13:28.130 --> 00:13:29.370
I’m being used!

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:31.130
Don’t lie!

00:13:31.130 --> 00:13:33.400
I just saw you
spread the virus!

00:13:33.400 --> 00:13:34.690
What are you doing?

00:13:34.690 --> 00:13:36.700
I’m tracking the criminal!

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:42.420
He’ll be at the location where he
accessed this computer from the outside!

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:43.980
Damn!

00:13:43.980 --> 00:13:47.950
I received a data file telling me to use this computer
to uncover the criminal’s identity.

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:52.390
I didn’t know it was an installation file to launch a virus bomb!

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:55.550
I unleashed a virus bomb
into the city!

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:58.370
I found him!

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:02.700
The virus bomb is active?

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:05.470
Yeah! I’ll capture the criminal!

00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:07.610
So you take care
of the bomb!

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:10.020
Wait, Yuma!

00:14:13.010 --> 00:14:14.250
Over there!

00:14:14.250 --> 00:14:17.040
The criminal is inside
that tower under construction!

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:21.040
Is the criminal really in here?

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:23.500
Yes, he must be here.

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:25.580
I’m surprised.

00:14:26.980 --> 00:14:29.990
You put it all together.

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:31.300
Mr. Ukyo?

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:33.560
Teacher, why are you here?

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:40.840
To summarize,
Mr. Ukyo is the criminal?

00:14:40.840 --> 00:14:42.840
You can say that.

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:45.030
Teacher, you must be kidding!

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:48.400
I expected the class representative
to find this location.

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:51.620
To summarize, this is a trap?

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:56.580
The virus bomb that you spread
will start working in 30 minutes.

00:14:56.580 --> 00:15:02.290
I wanted you to witness the moment
the virus bomb starts working.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:04.710
That makes me an accomplice!

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:10.640
A Number!

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:13.500
Observation #4:

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:16.560
This is not from this world.

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:21.020
It’s like a puzzle
with a hidden message.

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:24.890
What? Is there a Number?

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:30.820
Teacher...

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:33.070
That’s the mark of a Number.

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:36.120
I thought you went away!

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:37.410
I didn’t.

00:15:37.410 --> 00:15:39.980
But you weren’t here until now!

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:41.370
Yuma?

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:44.050
Why is he talking to himself?

00:15:44.050 --> 00:15:47.840
Did the ghost duelist arrive?

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:50.580
I’m ignoring you!

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:53.430
Teacher, why are doing
something so stupid?

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:56.390
I’m challenging myself.

00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:59.100
It’s the same as your kattobing.

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:00.660
It’s not the same!

00:16:00.660 --> 00:16:04.250
Causing trouble isn’t kattobing!

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:05.700
Yuma, you must duel.

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:09.990
A Number took over his soul.

00:16:10.420 --> 00:16:14.450
You can’t persuade him until you remove the Number from his body.

00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:18.010
Teacher, duel me!

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:21.290
If you lose, you have to
stop the virus bomb!

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:23.620
Duel!

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:24.980
Fine!

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:27.800
If you win, I’ll stop
the virus bomb!

00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:31.550
But are you good enough
to be my opponent?

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:33.900
I’ll show you my kattobing power!

00:16:33.900 --> 00:16:34.800
Let’s battle!

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:38.260
D-Gazer set!

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:40.140
Target locked on!

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:46.000
AR Vision Link complete.

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:48.190
Duel!

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:51.680
Do your best, Yuma!

00:16:51.680 --> 00:16:53.680
You must win!

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:55.990
Or else, I’ll be a criminal!

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:57.990
I go first!

00:16:57.990 --> 00:17:00.830
My turn! I draw!

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:04.580
I set a monster face-down
in defense position!

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:07.820
Facedown in defense position?

00:17:07.820 --> 00:17:10.340
What monster did he set?

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:13.010
I end my turn.

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:16.100
My turn! I draw!

00:17:16.100 --> 00:17:18.180
I summon Gagaga Magician!

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:27.400
What’s his set monster’s DEF?

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:31.050
There’s no point thinking about it!

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:32.190
Gagaga Magician!

00:17:32.560 --> 00:17:34.070
Attack it!

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:35.700
How lame.

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:39.810
Come, Crashbug X!

00:17:39.810 --> 00:17:41.610
Crashbug!

00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:46.370
2000 DEF!

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:50.270
Yuma’s monster is fine,
but he lost life points?

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:55.380
If you attack a monster with greater DEF,
the attacking monster isn’t destroyed.

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:57.640
But you subtract the ATK
from its DEF.

00:17:57.640 --> 00:18:00.600
To summarize, it’s 2000 minus 1500!

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:03.270
That’s 500 points of damage!

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:05.620
It’s my turn!

00:18:05.620 --> 00:18:06.730
I draw!

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:09.020
I summon Crashbug Y!

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:16.400
I activate the spell card
Crashbug Road from my hand!

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:22.580
Each player selects a Level
4-or-below monster on his field.

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:27.920
We can Special Summon a monster
from our hands that has the same Level.

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:31.590
I Special Summon Crashbug Z!

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:32.860
All right!

00:18:32.860 --> 00:18:37.880
Level 4 Gogogo Golem in my hand is
the same Level as Gagaga Magician.

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:39.790
I’ll summon Gogogo Golem—

00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:42.700
Yuma, summon it in defense position.

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:46.890
Due to Gogogo Golem’s effect,
it won’t be destroyed in battle once.

00:18:47.260 --> 00:18:50.860
I’m willing to duel,
but I won’t listen to you!

00:18:50.860 --> 00:18:55.430
I Special Summon Gogogo
Golem in attack position!

00:18:57.710 --> 00:18:58.780
How’s that!

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:02.990
Since it has 1800 ATK,
you can’t destroy it easily!

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:06.360
I’m now ready
for a perfect victory.

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:11.570
I overlay Level 3
Crashbug X, Y and Z!

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:18.330
With these three monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:19:23.390 --> 00:19:25.140
It’s coming.

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:28.140
An Xyz Monster using three monsters?

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:29.070
That’s right!

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:30.390
Xyz Summon!

00:19:30.390 --> 00:19:33.310
Appear, Number 34!

00:19:44.630 --> 00:19:47.120
Terror-Byte!

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:51.570
Number?

00:19:51.570 --> 00:19:53.880
What’s that monster?

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:55.420
Number...

00:19:58.010 --> 00:19:59.390
I have it!

00:20:01.330 --> 00:20:04.390
I also have Leviathan Dragon?

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:07.890
Huh? Is it because
he came back?

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:09.180
Here I go!

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:12.180
I activate Terror-Byte’s effect!

00:20:12.180 --> 00:20:20.880
Once per turn, I can use an Overlay Unit
to control your Level 4-or-below monster this turn.

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:27.240
This is my perfect dueling!

00:20:28.020 --> 00:20:30.080
My Gogogo Golem!

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:35.380
Go, Gogogo Golem!

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:43.510
Gagaga!

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:49.360
I finally managed to hack into the virus bomb program,
but where’s the activation switch?

00:20:55.200 --> 00:20:57.900
I have to find it
in this dungeon?

00:20:57.900 --> 00:21:00.360
And there’s a time limit.

00:21:01.060 --> 00:21:04.450
How do you like
my perfect dueling?

00:21:04.870 --> 00:21:08.700
Is perfection that important?

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:09.770
It is.

00:21:09.770 --> 00:21:11.790
Perfection is everything.

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:17.210
To achieve my own perfection,
I’m rewriting this city’s programs.

00:21:17.210 --> 00:21:19.670
There’s no way
a dunce can win!

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:23.060
So that’s how you really feel!

00:21:23.060 --> 00:21:24.170
It hurts.

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:26.160
Where does it hurt?

00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:27.390
My heart!

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:29.750
Observation #5:

00:21:29.750 --> 00:21:32.200
A human’s heart can be hurt.

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:33.350
I’ll remember that.

00:21:33.800 --> 00:21:38.450
Now, I also know the pain
of swallowing a sea lion.

00:21:38.450 --> 00:21:40.320
Yuma...

00:21:41.140 --> 00:21:43.710
This may be the wrong
time to say this...

00:21:43.710 --> 00:21:48.710
The phrase “to summarize” is derived
from a striped mullet growing into an adult.

00:21:48.710 --> 00:21:51.990
It means heading towards a destination.

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:54.480
What are you talking about?

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:57.280
I thought you were talking
about a sea lion!

00:21:57.280 --> 00:22:02.670
To summarize, it means
an idiot like you can’t win!

00:22:13.790 --> 00:22:16.350
Let’s start the duel!

00:22:17.050 --> 00:22:18.670
This week’s quiz:

00:22:18.670 --> 00:22:21.800
Monster Cards have stars.

00:22:21.800 --> 00:22:24.650
What do these stars represent?

00:22:30.460 --> 00:22:35.060
Today’s test is hard
Can’t avoid pleasure and temptation

00:22:35.060 --> 00:22:39.880
I want to go home and watch TV
Recent cartoons are entertaining

00:22:50.180 --> 00:22:54.680
Anyway, tests are hard
Language, math and English are especially hard

00:22:54.680 --> 00:22:59.480
Average scores in science and social studies
I’m only good at P.E.

00:22:59.480 --> 00:23:02.480
(Wait, Baby!) The expected

00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:04.780
(What’s that, Baby!) Answers

00:23:04.780 --> 00:23:07.550
(Wait a sec, Baby!) Remember them

00:23:07.550 --> 00:23:08.820
(What are we!? Baby!) For who

00:23:09.220 --> 00:23:13.860
Let’s say I wrote
the correct answers on that sheet

00:23:13.860 --> 00:23:18.040
Will that change the future a year
or a decade from now?

00:23:18.710 --> 00:23:23.810
The world I drew
at the edge of dreams

00:23:23.810 --> 00:23:28.720
Someday I’ll race in the sky

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:33.220
Nobody can threaten my heart

00:23:33.300 --> 00:23:37.390
Nothing is correct!

00:23:40.410 --> 00:23:41.730
Why?

00:23:41.730 --> 00:23:44.490
My teacher is
behind the virus bomb?

00:23:44.490 --> 00:23:46.400
And he’s also
possessed by a Number!

00:23:46.850 --> 00:23:49.620
Yuma, your dueling
isn’t good enough to defeat him.

00:23:49.620 --> 00:23:50.660
Be quiet!

00:23:50.660 --> 00:23:53.240
I won’t listen
to what you say!

00:23:53.240 --> 00:23:55.240
Hurry up! There’s no time left!

00:23:55.910 --> 00:23:59.820
I’m going to win this duel
and stop the virus bomb!

00:23:59.820 --> 00:24:00.960
But at this rate...

00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:09.970
Countdown to a Comeback! Astral is the Secret Plan?!

00:24:01.340 --> 00:24:03.450
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:

00:24:03.450 --> 00:24:06.380
“Countdown to a Comeback!
Astral is the Secret Plan?!”

00:24:06.830 --> 00:24:09.970
I’m kattobing!

00:24:10.470 --> 00:24:12.400
Here’s the answer!

00:24:12.920 --> 00:24:15.020
It’s the monster’s Level!

00:24:15.020 --> 00:24:19.240
Since it has 4 stars,
it’s Level 4.

00:24:19.240 --> 00:24:24.150
High-Level monsters seem exciting!
